# E2E fixtures. Keep out of every image build context -- prod doesn't need
# them, and the e2e stack bind-mounts them at runtime instead:
#   - `e2e/fixtures/fake-claude.sh` -> /usr/local/bin/claude (replaces the
#     real claude binary so tests don't need an API key)
#   - `e2e/fixtures` -> /app/e2e/fixtures (legacy mount, kept for any future
#     in-container reads; the current Mode A.1 entrypoint reads nothing
#     from here)
# Pre-Mode-A.1 this directory also contained `fake-claude-code-executor.mjs`
# which the entrypoint would install as an executor plugin when
# ARK_E2E_MODE=1. That gate has been removed (the tests now exercise the
# real claude-code executor end-to-end), but excluding `e2e/` from prod
# image builds stays correct as defense-in-depth.
#
# NB: NOT excluding **/__tests__/ or *.test.ts -- packages/core/services/
# actions/index.ts imports ./__tests__/flaky-pr-fixture.js as part of the
# ARK_ENABLE_TEST_ACTIONS=1 path. Pre-rolled images saw `Cannot find
# module './__tests__/flaky-pr-fixture.js'` and crashlooped.
e2e/
